 ### TypeScript boundary (clause 1; canonical)
 
-Product behavior is Rust only. Outside `tools/orchestration`, JS/TS source may live in exactly one place: `apps/desktop`'s webview frontend, which holds presentation only — everything it triggers is behavior in a workspace crate, reached through Tauri commands gated by capabilities under `apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/` (A14); capability files enumerate only the app's own commands, and the `fs`, `shell`, and `dialog` plugins are not enabled — file access happens in workspace crates, never through plugin scopes. Capability-based isolation assumes a patched framework, and this design carries no patch number for it: the desktop design pins the newest `tauri` release available when it lands in `[workspace.dependencies]` (never below 2.11.1) and checks Tauri's own repository advisory list — the crates.io/RustSec data the scheduled `cargo deny` scan reads does not carry every v2 advisory (A27). Node is only ever a prerequisite for that frontend's framework tooling (A15); the framework, bundler, and npm config are the desktop design's choice (deferred). The desktop-era `src-tauri` package's exact `members` path is likewise the desktop design's call.
